    "qid": "Q5",
    "answer": "Pemex places pressure on Mexico's public finances through several channels:\n\n- **Government Financial Support and Pre-Capitalized Notes:** Financial support operations for Pemex have involved the issuance of pre-capitalized notes amounting to about 0.6 percent of GDP, which are under discussion for inclusion in gross public debt.\n- **Supplier Debt Repayment:** The upcoming repayment of Pemex's supplier debt through the newly created Pemex Investment Fund may lead to an increase in the Debt Sustainability Analysis (DSA) stock of gross public debt, as accounts payable and supplier debt have historically been excluded from the gross public debt perimeter.\n- **Supplier Arrears:** Pemex accumulated arrears on supplier debt amounting to 0.6 percent of GDP at end-2024 (and 0.1 percent of GDP as of September 12, 2025), which are not included in the official net or gross stock of public sector borrowing requirements.",
